Z||000000||b lo 0||08-13-2001||12:36 AM||||I only have 2 major problems left.  One is the bad spark.  Search on the thread to see what the dillyo is-its a really long story.  In fact, it's so weak, I got whipped by a Golf tonight, and said, "That's it, I'm fixing it tomorrow."  Second is the intake hose keeps popping off the filter housing when it's running.  Is the filter bad?  It looks OK.  I jam that sucker on there, tighten the clamp, and it pops off by the time I get where I'm going.  That's major because stuff in your ingine gets expensive.  With the spark thing, the ICM, bobbin coil, ignition coil, cap, rotor, wires and plugs are all new.  I even checked the C500 like Ogre said.  Help?<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-13-2001||08:00 PM||||on a stock motor intake hose yanking off means the engine is moving too much... bad mount or dog bone. unless someone shortened the tube.<P>Don't go by the visible apearance of the spark. It's often very misleading. The only way to truly measure this is with a spark tester.<P>You need to work over all the wire. check everything in my cave wire service article. there are a number of things in there that could do it.<P>have you rechecked base timing? are you sure you did it right? incorrect timing will cause weak performance.||||reg||1
